                              SysOp Menu Help
                              ---------------


E - Edit User

    This command allows you edit any user.  You can change just about all
    information about him/her.

B - Ban User

    If you want to prevent a user from ever logging on again, use this
    command.

D - Delete User

    This will remove a user totally from the system.
    
F - Fumigate User List

    This will delete user's who haven't logged on since a certain date, and
    will also point out user's that need to be validated.

V - Validate Users

    This will look for all newly joined users, and prompt you whether or
    not to edit them, so that you can adjust their time, access, and other
    parameters.

L - Read Log

    Let's you read the SysOp's log book, which contains information on what
    callers have done.  Be sure to delete this regularily if you don't want
    it to get too big.

Q - Quit to Main Menu

    Takes you back to the Main Menu of the BBS.

U - User List

    Displays the user listing.  You can optionally get a verbose user
    listing, which will display all information about each user.  During
    the user listing, you can select Edit at any time to go into to edit
    mode for a user.

